1
00:00:00,152 --> 00:00:08,003
The notes in Tastebuds are written in a small editor field. Any web page can embed it. This is a first install.

2
00:00:08,569 --> 00:00:16,206
Clone the repository, install, and build the field. Measured on one machine, the three commands took under five seconds.

3
00:00:16,824 --> 00:00:20,002
The page needs three things. A stylesheet.

4
00:00:20,034 --> 00:00:23,042
An empty element, for the field to build in.

5
00:00:23,075 --> 00:00:27,896
And one call: createEditor, with that element and the text to start with.

6
00:00:27,927 --> 00:00:32,493
Listen for change, and the page gets the new text after every edit.

7
00:00:33,037 --> 00:00:37,111
Here is that page. The field opens with its starting notes.

8
00:00:37,179 --> 00:00:40,187
Type, and the text below follows every key.

9
00:00:40,229 --> 00:00:44,432
Two stars make a word bold as you type. So does control B.

10
00:00:44,462 --> 00:00:46,873
A dash and a space start a list.

11
00:00:46,882 --> 00:00:53,858
What the page receives is plain text: a small subset of Markdown, easy to read and easy to store.

12
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:59,476
createEditor makes the field. destroy removes it. The guide has the rest.
